        <p class="about-text">
          I was born in Nairobi, Kenya, in a big family of eight kids. My parents always worked hard for us to
          have a better life, which gave me the morals of hard work and not giving up when things get tough. I
          was always fascinated with airplanes growing up, which took me to Western Michigan University to study
          Aeronautical Engineering — my passion for how things are designed, tested, and made carried straight
          into a decade of manufacturing and tooling simulation work at G-TEKT, Tesla, and Rivian.
        </p>
        <p class="about-text">
